xnu 0288: the touch event is published in the first millisecond of the tick

0286 samples the display tick after the drain so that one event comes out per
tick, and that part works: `ev 60/s` at 14-19 ms spacings. But it also moved the
publish to the end of the drain, and the framebuffer woke the report thread at
the end of its tick, after the panel copy. The event then reached the UI 5-8 ms
into the period, and the compositor's commit missed its slot: with the touch
rate, the event rate and the panel tick all unchanged (348/s, 60/s, 60 Hz), the
frames went from `late avg 5.7 ms, 15-18 ms apart` (60 fps) to `late avg 10 ms`
with one frame every two to three periods, and the user saw it as jerks.

The wake now goes out right after the clients are told and before the copy, so
the report thread runs while the tick copies the panel, and the publish happens
as soon as the first report of the wake is read. The rest of the drain still
runs and its position belongs to the next tick, which keeps one event per tick
and still gives a touch-down its own event.

